Krita Nova 30 - dialogs without the white border (Android)

Krita's Android Qt draws a white frame around every decorated window, so the
dialogs (Levels and the other filters, layer properties, message boxes ...)
had a white border. Like the brush editor (patches 11 and 23), they now have
no platform frame but a look of their own:

- rounded corners (8 px) and a grey 1.5 px outline, in the dialog's colour;
- a title bar in the same colour: the dialog's title in the middle and an
  "x" on the right (closes the dialog like Cancel); dragging the title bar
  moves the dialog;
- dragging its edges resizes it (FloatingDockResizer, patch 14, now also
  handles these dialogs).

KisTouchFriendlyStyle.cpp, DialogFramer (installed with the Android style):
when a QDialog with a layout is polished - right before it is first shown -
it gets FramelessWindowHint and a translucent background. If its platform
window was already created (but not yet shown), that window is dropped and
created again, frameless and with an alpha channel, when the dialog is shown,
and the dialog gets a new backing store for it. A DialogFrame adds the title
bar above the dialog's layout (whose margins make room for it) and paints the
rounded background. Popups, tooltips, splash screens and windows that are
already frameless are left alone.
